{# THE AREA SETTINGS SECTION — what this area is, and what an installation may
   change about it.

   A SECTION, NOT A SCREEN. It carries no page frame, no head, no strip and no
   way back: the shell's configure page draws all four, and the area's Configure
   action is both the way in and the way out. Before the frame this was a screen
   of its own with a tab in the area's strip, which put "what this area is" beside
   "what is happening in it" as though the two were the same kind of place.

   GATED ON `areas.configure`, ASKED OF THE AREA by the declaration that lists
   this section, so reaching the section at all is the permission. The page states what is editable and what is not rather than
   offering fields that do nothing: the boundary is not re-drawn here, because
   importing one is a surface this bundle does not ship yet and pretending
   otherwise would be a form that fails on submit.

   THE SHEET IS LINKED HERE, IN THE BODY, and that is deliberate rather than
   sloppy: a section is included into a page the shell owns, and the shell's head
   cannot know which bundle's vocabulary the section is written in. A stylesheet
   link in the body is applied exactly as one in the head is; what it costs is
   that this section's own rules land a beat after the frame's. #}
{{ include('@Area/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{#- Where these values are set: a link for whoever may read Settings. -#}
{%- set _setIn = door('settings.read')
    ? '<a class="chip" href="' ~ path('settings_core')|e('html_attr') ~ '">set in Settings &rsaquo; Core</a>'
    : '<span class="chip">set in Settings &rsaquo; Core</span>' -%}
<div class="grid">
        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">The record<span class="src">&middot; area_of_interest</span></span>

            {# READ-ONLY HERE, EDITED ON ITS OWN SCREEN. The record below is the
               lead; the one action is the door to the edit screen — including the
               boundary, which is never re-drawn on this page. #}
            <div class="id-head">
                <span class="id-lead">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect width="18" height="11" x="3" y="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
                    <span><b>Read-only here.</b> These facts are edited on their own screen &mdash; including the boundary.</span>
                </span>
                <a class="cta id-edit" href="{{ path('area_edit', {uuid: area.uuidString}) }}">
                    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 20h9"/><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.12 2.12 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4Z"/></svg> Edit area
                </a>
            </div>

            <table class="tbl">
                <tr><th>Name</th><td>{{ area.name }}</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Boundary source</th><td>{% if area.hasBoundary %}{{ area.source }}{% else %}<span class="chip">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Size</th><td class="num">{{ areaKm2|number_format }} km&sup2;</td></tr>
                <tr><th>Zones</th><td class="num">{{ zoneCount > 0 ? zoneCount : '—' }}</td></tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>IUCN category</th>
                    <td>{% if area.iucnCategory %}{{ area.iucnCategory }}{% else %}<span class="chip">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Established</th>
                    <td>{% if area.establishedYear %}{{ area.establishedYear }}{% else %}<span class="chip">&mdash;</span>{% endif %}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Zone overlap tolerance</th>
                    <td class="num">{{ zoneTolerance }} % {{ _setIn|raw }}</td>
                </tr>
                {# HOW OFTEN THIS AREA'S HANDSETS REPORT, AND WHEN A SILENT ONE
                   GOES STALE — the values in force here, read-only. Super
                   Admins and Admins set them in Settings › Core, for the
                   organization or customised for this area. #}
                <tr>
                    <th>Ping every</th>
                    <td class="num">{{ pingEvery }} {{ _setIn|raw }}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <th>Stale after</th>
                    <td class="num">{{ staleAfter }}{% if staleIsTwoPings %} <span class="chip">two pings</span>{% endif %} {{ _setIn|raw }}</td>
                </tr>
                <tr><th>Identifier</th><td class="mono">{{ area.uuidString }}</td></tr>
            </table>
            <div class="use">The registry fields are optional and a dash means UNRECORDED, not zero:
                an installation that drew its own boundary has no IUCN category and no gazettement
                year, and must not be made to invent them to save a record.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

{# THE CHECK-IN STATUSES — the AREA's list of the words a ranger checks in with
   (uhifadhi-web/areas/kilimani/configure/index.html#check-in-statuses). One row
   per status, the offered ones in handset order, then the ones not offered.
   The label is reworded freely; the key is fixed once saved, because the phone
   sends it and every check-in carries it; the kind is one of the platform's
   four, fixed once the status has check-ins; a status is deactivated, never
   deleted, and one not offered is frozen until reactivated.

   THE ROWS ARE DRAWN BY THE CONTROLLER from the model below — the list as
   stored with each status's "used", the four kinds in the platform's words,
   and after a refused save the list as it was sent — and the whole list posts
   at once through the settings save bar, as statuses[i][key|label|kind|active|new]. #}
{%- set _cis = checkInStatuses -%}
<form class="cis-wrap" id="check-in-statuses" method="post" action="{{ _cis.action }}" data-controller="uhifadhi--area-bundle--check-in-statuses">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ _cis.token }}" data-token="area_check_in_statuses">
    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">Check-in statuses<span class="src">&middot; duty_checkin_status</span><span class="src" data-cis-count></span></span>
        <p class="cx-note cis-lead">What a ranger can answer on checking in, in the order the handset offers it. The words are this area&rsquo;s own; each one means one of four things the platform counts.</p>
        <div class="dw-scroll"><table class="tbl cis"><thead><tr><th class="sorted">Order</th><th>Status &middot; what a ranger reads</th><th>Kind &middot; what it means</th><th>Offered</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
        <div class="use"><b>The phone sends the key, not the label.</b> A label can be reworded at any time; a key is fixed once saved, because every check-in already made carries it and a new key would leave them behind. <b>A key is used once in this area</b>, offered or not. <b>A kind is fixed once a status has check-ins</b> &mdash; they read by it; add a new status to mean something else. <b>At least one At a station status stays offered</b> &mdash; it is the only kind that names a station. <b>Deactivate, never delete:</b> a status no longer offered keeps every check-in made with it.</div>
        <div class="staddrow"><button type="button" class="btn sm" data-act="add">Add a status</button><span class="sp"></span><span class="cx-why">phones pick up a change at their next sync</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ed-bar{% if _cis.refusal %} refused{% endif %}" role="status"><b>{{ _cis.refusal ?: (_cis.justSaved ? 'Saved' : 'No unsaved changes') }}</b><span class="cx-why"></span><span class="sp"></span><button type="button" class="ed-btn ghost" disabled>Discard</button><button type="button" class="ed-btn" data-review disabled>Review &#9652;</button><button type="submit" class="ed-btn pri" disabled>Save</button></div>
    <div class="c ed-reviewcard" hidden><span class="tab">Review<span class="src"></span></span><ul class="ed-review"></ul></div>
    <template data-cis-icon="up">{{ ux_icon('shell:chevron-up') }}</template>
    <template data-cis-icon="down">{{ ux_icon('shell:chevron-down') }}</template>
    <script type="application/json" data-cis-model>{{ _cis.model|json_encode(constant('JSON_HEX_TAG') b-or constant('JSON_HEX_AMP') b-or constant('JSON_UNESCAPED_UNICODE') b-or constant('JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES'))|raw }}</script>
</form>
